+### Semantic checks in CI
+
+An explicit `--baseline-only` check uses this same entrypoint and executes both
+complete unmutated oracle passes, including every fixed/random campaign,
+construction, reach check, calibration and determinism check. It records the
+same captures and seed controls, then ends before selected-suffix validation and
+mutation execution. It refuses mutant/diff/owner selectors.
+
+This mode is for a maintainer-chosen per-change semantic CI gate. Its report says
+`purpose: "baseline-only"`, marks the mutation audit `not-run`, and ends with
+`done baseline-completed`; it never reports zero gaps. It cannot replace the full
+gap check when adopting/changing oracles, evaluating missing sensitivity, removing
+old coverage, or claiming gap closure. Keep a separate full check for those gates.
